   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by hand. The stereochemistry is the least certain part, because several wedge and hash bonds were hard to make out.\n\n**Peptide core, read from the N-terminus:**\n- Ac-D-Arg, then Pen, Asn, Thr, 7-methyl-Trp, Lys(Ac), Pen. The two Pen residues are joined by an S\u2013S bond that closes the macrocycle.\n- Then Tyr with an O-CH2CH2NH2 ether, 2-naphthylalanine, and the cyclopentane amino acid (Ac5c).\n- Then Glu, Asn, the 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid residue (Thp), and a C-terminal Lys-NH2.\n\n**Lys side chain, running to the lipid:**\n- Lys side-chain NH, then two repeats of C(=O)CH2-O-CH2CH2-O-CH2CH2-NH.\n- Then \u03b3-Glu, whose \u03b1-NH is acylated by an octadecanedioic acid. The diacid has 16 CH2 groups, counted from the drawing and not certain.\n\n**Stereochemistry from the wedge and hash bonds:**\n- L: Pen (both), Asn (both), Thr, Trp, Lys(Ac), Glu and the linker \u03b3-Glu.\n- D: Arg and the Tyr derivative.\n- 2-Nal is L. Its bond looked hashed, which I read as L.\n- The second Asn's wedge was ambiguous, so I assigned L as the more likely default.\n- Thr's \u03b2-carbon follows standard L-Thr.\n- The Lys \u03b1-carbon and the Ac5c and Thp quaternary carbons carry no stereo.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@H](CCCNC(=N)N)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1c[nH]c2c(C)cccc12)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)S%10)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc1ccc(OCCN)cc1)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc1ccc2ccccc2c1)C(=O)NC1(CCCC1)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(=O)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)NC1(CCOCC1)C(=O)NC(CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](NC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCCCCCC(=O)O)C(=O)O)C(N)=O"
